# Every token kind the host lexer can produce, for M18a parity.
# Not a valid program — only the kinds are compared.
#
# Two of the host's kinds are absent and cannot be added: `Eof`, which the test
# drops from both streams, and `Hash`, which no source can produce because `#`
# is always consumed as a line comment before a token is cut.
"""
A block comment is trivia, not a string.
"""
async await break const continue copy defer drop else elif enum err extern
false fn for give if impl in match module mut new none not ok parallel pub
raise ref return self some spawn struct throws trait true type unsafe use
void while as test bench expect

plain_ident _under x9

0 42 1_000 0xFF 0XfF 0b1010 0B11
3.14 1e9 2E-7 6.02e+23 1_0.5_0

"text" "with {interp} inside" "nested {f("q")} quote" "esc \" and \n"
'a' '\n' '\\' '\x41'
b"bytes" b"esc \x00"

+ - * / % = == != < <= > >= && || ! ? ?? & | ^ ~ << >>
. .. ..= ... -> => , : ; ( ) [ ] { } @
0..3

$ `
